Looks aren't everything. She looks a little dopey to me.

163
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,280
你喜欢聪明的女人？
So, your ideal woman should be intelligent?

164
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:08,840
是的，我喜欢聪明的女人.
Yeah, I like an intellectual woman...

165
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:17,860
她必须懂得浪漫.
but she should be romantic, too...

166
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,820
但不能太得意忘形
but not take herself too seriously.

167
00:11:27,412 --> 00:11:30,583
-就是这样! -还有什么？
- Yeah, like that! - What else?

168
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,680
等等
Wait a minute.

169
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,980
你有心上人吗？
You have somebody specific in mind, don't you?

170
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:37,060
-有 -莱斯莉!
- Yes. - Leslie!

171
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:40,640
-莱斯莉？ -杰夫？
- Leslie? - Jeffrey!

172
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:45,460
-杰夫？ -民工杰夫!是你
- Jeffrey? - Jeffrey, Jeffrey, Jeffrey Backman! It's you.

173
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:47,860
莱斯莉，真不敢相信 还以为你在伦敦呢？
Leslie, I don't believe this. I thought you we're in London!

174
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:51,080
是的，但我和演艺老师吵架
Yes, well, I got in a fight with my acting coach.

175
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:54,680
他坚持让我穿短背心演麦克白 [莎翁名剧]
He insisted I play Lady Macbeth in a tank top.

176
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:55,680
-这样演我会去看! -你当然了
- Hey, I'd go! - I'm sure, you would.

177
00:11:58,700 --> 00:12:01,360
-对不起，这是.. -凯罗!
- I'm sorry. Leslie, this is-- - Carol!

178
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,540
凯罗.西弗，这是莱斯莉
Carol Seaver. Carol, this is Leslie Berenson.

179
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,240
凯罗是我亲戚，我把她当作妹妹
Carol's an old family friend, she's like the little sister I never had.

180
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:09,040
太好了
That's sweet.

181
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:14,000
-凯罗，念几年级了？ -初三
- What grade are you in, in school, Carol? - Ninth.

182
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:18,060
失陪了，我去洗手间
If you'll excuse me, I have to go to the bathroom.

183
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:29,238
麦姬，我听到声音了 咱自然点
Maggie, I think I hear them. Let's try to act natural.

184
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:34,040
嗨，甜心
Hi, honey.

185
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,460
-嗨，妈妈!爸爸! -嗨!
- Hi, Mom! Hi, Dad! - Hi.

186
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,960
我去睡了!
Well, I'm off to bed now!

187
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:44,500
等等，戏好看吗？
Wait, honey, how was the show?

188
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:49,762
戏？戏很好看!
Show? The show was great!

189
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:53,400
-晚安 -凯罗？
- Well, good night! - Carol?

190
00:12:55,333 --> 00:12:57,332
-什么事？ -杰夫呢？
- Yeah, Dad? - Wheres Jeff?

191
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:04,460
天哪!把他锁在外面了!
Oh, my goodness! I must have locked him out!

192
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:12,220
杰夫，对不起
Jeffrey, I'm so sorry.

193
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,200
一下子忘了你
I guess I just forgot about you!

194
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:20,020
最后50步没有冲刺，是我的错
Well, it's really my fault for not wanting to sprint that last 50 yards.

195
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:24,540
对!晚安!
Right! Well, nighty-night!

196
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:29,605
凯罗!
Carol!

197
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:36,940
请听我解释.
I think I can explain.

198
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,360
就这样了
Well, I guess that's it.

199
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:47,020
孩子们，帮杰夫提行李上车
Hey, kids, why don't you help Jeff get his bags in the car?

200
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,340
-好吧，大的给我! -给我!大的给我!
- Okay. I get the big one! - No, I want the big one!

201
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:53,660
好吧，看在你是我弟弟的份上
Okay. But only because you're my brother and I love you.

202
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:58,360
屡试不爽!
Works every time!

203
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:02,540
替我跟凯罗道别
Be sure to say goodbye to Carol for me.

204
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:05,380
昨晚真是遗憾
I really feel terrible about last night.

205
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:07,320
杰夫，我们说了很多次了
Jeff, how many times do we have to tell you?

206
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:08,300
这不是你的错
It's not your fault.

207
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:10,800
凯罗有点过火了，但她坚强得很
Carol gets a little carried away, but she's resilient.

208
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:13,300
伤心过后她会马上跳回正轨
She gets hurt, she bounces right back.

209
00:14:16,414 --> 00:14:20,051
-弹跳力好 -杰夫!
- That's bouncy. - Jeffrey!

210
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:22,540
幸好赶得上你离开!
I'm so glad I caught you before you left!

211
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:26,480
这是我的“另一半”理查德
I'd like you to meet Richard, my "significant other."

212
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:29,640
-理查德，幸会 -什么“另一半”？
- Pleasure to meet you, Richard. - Significant other what?

213
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:34,680
理查德刚从巴黎回来
Richies been out of town. Just flew in from Paris.

214
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:41,120
去巴黎干什么了？
Now, what we're you doing in Paris, Richie?

215
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:46,540
出差
I was on business.

216
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:51,080
做盛行？
What do you do, Richie?

217
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:53,240
他是送报的!
He's our paper boy!

218
00:14:55,152 --> 00:14:57,185
送这么远!
Well, that's some route.

219
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:01,660
杰夫，再见[法语]!
Well, au revoir, Jeff!

220
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:04,940
有空来坐坐
Do come back and visit soon.

221
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:08,960
我要和理查德上楼去，好好叙旧
Richie and I will be upstairs. We have so much catching up to do!

222
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:18,760
我们就喜欢这一套
We're so this way.

223
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:26,760
太棒了!
This is incredible!

224
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,300
今天来收报纸.
I come here to collect for the paper...

225
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,000
竟然发现了浪漫
and I find romance.

226
00:15:38,129 --> 00:15:41,573
爱情总是那么的突如其来
But then, they say it comes when you least expect it.

227
00:15:44,268 --> 00:15:47,643
放开我!滚!
Get off of me! Get out of here!

228
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:51,200
不是那边，这边
Not that way. This way.

229
00:15:58,460 --> 00:15:59,960
这是二楼
We're on the second floor.

230
00:16:02,353 --> 00:16:06,500
那里有水管，发挥你的想象力，滚!
There's a ledge and a drain pipe. Use your imagination. Now, out!

231
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:07,280
好吧，我走了
All right, I'm going.

232
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:15,680
等等!你是在试验我的爱？
Wait! Is this a test of my love for you?

233
00:16:17,868 --> 00:16:20,640
是的，请离!
Sure. Now please, go!

234
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:27,560
我真是个混蛋!
I am such a jerk!

235
00:16:35,386 --> 00:16:36,486
嗨
Hi.

236
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:40,440
-理查德呢？ -被我扔出去了
- Wheres Richie? - I threw him out.

237
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:44,480
-扔到哪里？ -外面
- Out where? - Out there.

238
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:49,320
别着急，他爬树很了得
Don't worry, he climbs like a squirrel.

239
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:55,540
你们的关系进展真快
Well, sounds like you two have a pretty stormy relationship.

240
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:59,180
拜托，我和理查德根本没有关系!
Come off it, Dad, you know Richie and I don't have a relationship!

241
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:03,660
只是假装他是我男朋友 以此来气杰夫
I just pretended he was my boyfriend so I could get back at Jeff!

242
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:09,587
-宝贝.. -杰夫肯定认为.
- Sweetheart-- - Jeff must think I'm the biggest...

243
00:17:09,587 --> 00:17:11,358
我是个大傻瓜!
doofus he's ever seen!

244
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:13,980
不，杰夫不会认为你是个傻瓜
No, Carol, Jeff does not think you're a doofus.

245
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:18,020
而是一个漂亮，聪明的女孩子.
He thinks you're a beautiful, intelligent young woman...

246
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:21,100
只可惜太年幼了
who just happens to be a little too young for him.

247
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:22,560
也许吧
Yeah, sure.

248
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:27,260
这是他亲口说的 他今早很难过
Carol, that's what he said. He feels terrible about the whole thing.

249
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,420
每个人都会曾经冲动
Everybody acts a little crazy sometimes, you know.

250
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:31,540
冲动不代表是混蛋
That doesn't mean you're a jerk.

251
00:17:32,410 --> 00:17:35,720
-冲动是真情流露 -说得对
- it just means you follow your heart. - That's right, honey.

252
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:40,000
其实你爸爸.
In fact, your father...

253
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:45,100
他在初一生物女老师面前也出过洋相
made a major bozo of himself over his seventh-grade biology teacher.

254
00:17:46,991 --> 00:17:49,593
-是吗？你做些什么了？ -我没做什么.
- Yeah? What'd you do? - I didn't do anything--

255
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:51,140
拜托!
Oh, come on!

256
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:53,760
我的做法有点尴尬.
Well, mines a little embarrassing....

257
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:59,480
我绑架了她的仓鼠.
I kidnapped her hamsters and threatened to flush them...

258
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,500
要挟她不能嫁给社会老师
if she married Mr. Sprinkleman, the shop teacher.

259
00:18:03,274 --> 00:18:07,013
-这你没告诉我 -不是真的
- You didn't tell me that. - You didn't really do that.

260
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:11,800
真的!我往头上套个袋子.
I really did! Then I put a bag over my head...

261
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:15,380
站在她的窗外唱 <爱我就要付出代价>呢
and I stood outside her window and sang, That's What You Get For Lovin' Me.

262
00:18:17,421 --> 00:18:20,865
-是吗？ -你真像个傻瓜!
- You didn't? - You must have looked like a real doofus!

263
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:23,720
那是我最要命的一次
It happens to be one of my best numbers.

264
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:28,720
我相信在“傻瓜”这个行列.
Well, I'm sure your mother's not exactly an innocent in the...

265
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,280
你妈妈也逃不了
doofus-for-love department!

266
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:33,660
是吗？你做了些什么？
Yeah? What have you done?

267
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:38,000
我的傻事太多了.
Well, honey, I've done so many silly things....

268
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,960
-数也数不清 -就挑一件吧
- I couldn't possibly list them all. - Come on, just pick one.

269
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,560
对，最傻的一件
Yeah. The silliest.

270
00:18:46,183 --> 00:18:48,819
好吧，让我想想
Well, okay. Let's see.

271
00:18:50,287 --> 00:18:51,284
好
Okay.

272
00:18:51,689 --> 00:18:56,691
我有一次写了张纸条：“你真帅”
Okay. Once I wrote a note that said:

273
00:18:57,420 --> 00:19:01,840
递给一个我不认识的男孩
"I think you're cute, " to a boy I didn't even know.

274
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,860
这就是最傻的事？
That's the silliest thing you ever did?

275
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:12,860
你妈妈就是那么滑稽
Your mother's a pretty zany lady, Carol.

276
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:18,740
也许吧，你是说这是遗传病？
So, I guess, you're trying to tell me, this problem is genetic.

277
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:22,560
-妈妈？ -什么事？
- Mom? - Yeah, sweetheart?

278
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:29,360
杰夫真的说我漂亮.
Did Jeff really say that he thinks that I'm beautiful...

279
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:30,680
而且聪明？
and intelligent?

280
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:35,180
他真的这么说
He really said that.

281
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:37,560
你若是能下去道别.
And I think he'd appreciate it...

282
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:39,740
他会很高兴的
if you went downstairs and said goodbye to him.

283
00:19:40,204 --> 00:19:43,079
-他还在？ -他说会等你
- He's still here? - He said he'd wait for you.

284
00:19:43,874 --> 00:19:45,247
是吗？
Yeah?

285
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:49,000
有没有说等多久？
Did he say how long?

286
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:07,000
-嗨 -嗨
- Hi. - Hi.

287
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:11,980
理查德远从巴黎回来.
I really appreciate you coming down to say goodbye...

288
00:20:12,136 --> 00:20:15,170
很感谢你还能下来道别
what with Richie coming in from Paris and all.

289
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:18,060
这个.
Yeah, well...

290
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:23,100
我们说好了 他准许我跟别的男人说再见
Richie and I have an understanding. He let's me say goodbye to other men.

291
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:30,154
凯罗，若是我不小心伤害了你 真的对不起
Look, Carol, if I hurt you in any way, I'm really sorry.

292
00:20:30,154 --> 00:20:31,891
-我只是.. -别担心，我.
- I just want-- - Don't worry about it. I mean...

293
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,760
我们也玩得很开心
we had some good times.

294
00:20:34,325 --> 00:20:37,461
-夫复何求？ -是啊
- What more can you ask for from life? - Yeah.

295
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:41,980
希望你能改观
Well, if it makes any difference...

296
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:46,180
若我们都是14岁，我也会爱得疯狂
if we we're both 14, I'd be one lovesick puppy.

297
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:50,240
-是吗？ -是的
- Really? - Really.

298
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:58,000
若我们都23岁就好玩了
Imagine how fun it would be if we we're both 23.

299
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:07,000
我23岁时，你已经32岁
Well, maybe when I'm 23 and you're 32.

300
00:21:07,825 --> 00:21:10,063
你32岁时，我41岁
Or when you're 32 and I'm 41.

301
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:14,634
我风华正茂 我才看不上你这老头
Hey, I'm not gonna be wanting to date any old geezers in the prime of my life.

302
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:19,280
-若我是个有钱的老头呢？ -那就说说看
- What if I'm a rich old geezer? - We'll talk.

303
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:28,260
凯罗，我觉得你很特别
You know, you're very special, Carol.

304
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:32,680
你很快就能碰到.
Pretty soon you're gonna bump into some lucky guy your own age...

305
00:21:32,783 --> 00:21:34,452
能懂得你的同龄人
who's going to find that out.

306
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:38,040
凯罗，再见
Bye, Carol.

307
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:40,900
大笨蛋，再见
Bye, Spudbrain.

308
00:21:56,006 --> 00:21:59,211
-理查德! -我.
- Richie! - Well....

309
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,160
我应该离开吧？
Guess I should be going, huh?

310
00:22:03,320 --> 00:22:07,540
理查德，我那么没礼貌，对不起
Oh, Richie. I'm sorry I was so rude to you.

311
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:10,620
-希望你能原谅我 -没关系
- I hope you can forgive me. - That's okay.

312
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:13,340
那是我人生中最美好的时光
This was the best day of my life.

313
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:19,580
-你真好人，谢谢 -嗯
- You're sweet. Thanks for everything. - Sure.

314
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:26,560
我忍不住说句，刚才无意中听到.
You know, I couldn't help but overhear what Jeff was saying about...

315
00:22:27,071 --> 00:22:31,140
什么幸运的同龄人，而我刚好14岁.
some lucky guy your own age and I just thought since I am 14--

316
00:22:31,208 --> 00:22:32,843
走吧!
Go!

317
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:37,453
男人啊
Men.

318
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:43,560
预备!开始!麦克，进攻!
Ready! Set! Tito, Michael, Jermaine! Hike!

319
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:49,020
-我没人防! -你们非得要打烂东西才高兴？
- I'm open! - Hey, you guys really won't be happy...

320
00:22:49,020 --> 00:22:52,700
好吧，比赛停止，对不起
- until something gets broken, will you? - All right. Time out. I'm sorry.

321
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:53,380
妈妈对!
Mother's right!

322
00:23:02,339 --> 00:23:03,871
开球!开球!
Hut! Hut!

323
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:53,586
[zeroxia@gmail.com] 2006.03.12
